@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating Resources with Azure DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Azure DevOps provides a seamless way to create and manage cloud infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code (IaC). This ensures automated, consistent, and scalable deployments.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why Automate Resource Creation?</h2>
        <p>Manually creating Azure resources can lead to **configuration drift, inefficiencies, and human errors**. Using Azure DevOps, we can:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Automate resource provisioning.</li>
            <li>Ensure **consistency and reproducibility**.</li>
            <li>Enable **version control** for infrastructure.</li>
            <li>Integrate with **CI/CD pipelines** for seamless deployments.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/create-resources.png" alt="Creating Resources in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Automating resource creation using Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Commonly Automated Resources</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Virtual Machines (VMs)</li>
                <li>Storage Accounts</li>
                <li>App Services</li>
                <li>Databases (SQL, CosmosDB)</li>
                <li>Networking (VNETs, Load Balancers)</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Step-by-Step: Creating Resources with Azure DevOps</h2>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Set up a Repository:</strong> Store your ARM/Terraform files in Azure Repos or GitHub.</li>
            <li><strong>Create a Build Pipeline:</strong> Validate infrastructure code (optional).</li>
            <li><strong>Define a Release Pipeline:</strong> Deploy the infrastructure to Azure.</li>
            <li><strong>Use Service Connections:</strong> Authenticate Azure DevOps with Azure.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor & Validate:</strong> Use logs, alerts, and monitoring tools.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Example YAML for Deploying Resources</h4>
            <pre>
stages:
- stage: DeployResources
  displayName: 'Deploy Resources to Azure'
  jobs:
  - job: TerraformApply
    steps:
    - task: TerraformTaskV2
      inputs:
        provider: 'azurerm'
        command: 'apply'
        workingDirectory: '$(Build.SourcesDirectory)/infra'
            </pre>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/iac-deployment.png" alt="IaC Deployment in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Infrastructure Deployment in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **parameterized templates** for flexibility.</li>
            <li>Implement **role-based access control (RBAC)**.</li>
            <li>Leverage **deployment approvals** to prevent unauthorized changes.</li>
            <li>Monitor deployments using **Azure Monitor & Log Analytics**.</li>
            <li>Test changes in **staging environments** before deploying to production.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Automating resource creation with Azure DevOps simplifies infrastructure management, reduces errors, and enhances scalability. Integrating IaC with pipelines enables fast, repeatable, and secure deployments.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Managing Environments with Azure DevOps** for handling multiple deployment environments efficiently.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("ARMvsTerraform", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: ARM Templates vs Terraform</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("ManageEnvironments", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Managing Environments with Azure DevOps &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
